---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
const n = site.name;
const toc = [
  { id: 'provider', label: 'Your AI provider and model' },
  { id: 'uses', label: 'Where AI is used' },
  { id: 'what', label: 'What is sent to the AI' },
  { id: 'limits', label: 'Limits of AI replies' },
  { id: 'controls', label: 'Controls you keep' },
  { id: 'people', label: 'People stay in charge' },
  { id: 'disclosure', label: 'Telling your customers' },
];
---

<Legal
  title="AI transparency"
  description={`How AI works in ${n}: workspaces choose their own AI provider and model, what content is sent, where AI is used, its limits and the controls you keep.`}
  intro={`${n} can use AI to suggest or write replies to customer messages, and to help your team understand conversations. This page explains who provides the AI, what it sees, and where its limits are.`}
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="provider" class="!mt-0">Your AI provider and model</h2>
  <p>
    {n} does not force one AI model on every customer. Each workspace selects and configures its own AI provider, credentials and model from
    the options {n} supports: Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Gemini, OpenRouter, and self-hosted models through Ollama or any OpenAI-compatible
    endpoint. {n} provides the inbox, routing, settings and controls around it.
  </p>
  <p>Each AI provider has its own terms, including whether it may use data to improve its models. Workspace owners should review the terms of the provider they choose.</p>

  <h2 id="uses">Where AI is used</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>AI replies:</strong> answering customers from the knowledge base when no rule matches, automatically or as a draft.</li>
    <li><strong>Copilot:</strong> summaries, suggested next steps, suggested replies and rewrites for your team. Copilot never sends anything itself.</li>
    <li><strong>Conversation Learning:</strong> finding recurring questions, proposing rules and building knowledge from past conversations.</li>
    <li><strong>Mood detection:</strong> noticing when a customer is upset or urgent so a person can step in. Alerts show structured reasons, not AI reasoning.</li>
    <li><strong>Social Studio:</strong> drafting post captions that a person reviews and approves.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Each of these is a separate module that the workspace can switch off.</p>

  <h2 id="what">What is sent to the AI</h2>
  <p>When a workspace turns on AI features, {n} sends the selected provider only what the task needs:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the customer’s message and relevant earlier messages in the conversation;</li>
    <li>the parts of the workspace’s knowledge base that relate to the question;</li>
    <li>for Copilot, the draft text the agent asks it to rewrite.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="limits">Limits of AI replies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>AI replies can be wrong, incomplete or out of date, even with a good knowledge base.</li>
    <li>The AI only knows what is in the conversation and the knowledge base.</li>
    <li>AI replies are not legal, medical, financial or safety advice, and should not be used for it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="controls">Controls you keep</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Choose whether AI drafts replies for review or sends them itself.</li>
    <li>Set the confidence AI needs before it answers. Below it, the conversation is handed to a person with the reason.</li>
    <li>Rate limits and cooldowns apply to every automatic reply, and a kill switch stops automation in a project at once.</li>
    <li>Test changes in the AI sandbox before customers see them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="people">People stay in charge</h2>
  <p>A person on the business’s team can take over a conversation at any time, with the earlier messages still in view. The business decides how AI is used in its workspace and is responsible for replies sent from it.</p>

  <h2 id="disclosure">Telling your customers</h2>
  <p>Where the law or a platform’s rules require it, businesses must tell their customers that replies may be generated by AI. This includes Meta’s rules for automated messaging on WhatsApp, Messenger and Instagram.</p>
  <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email.contact}`}>{site.email.contact}</a></p>
</Legal>
